⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
329 calories 24g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins included)

One Love Protein Ice Cream 😋🍦

Original recipe from my Recipe Book

Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Books with over 145 recipes like this one!

- 400g Fat Free @fairlife
- 40g Monk Fruit Sweetener (or any sugar substitute)
- 1 medium size banana (~100g)
- 5g (1 tsp) vanilla bean paste (or extract)
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 15g chocolate chips + 2g coconut oil
• Right before the Mix-In cycle, combine 15g of chocolate with 2g of coconut oil, melt in the microwave (30 sec intervals, stirring in between), hollow out a hole in the center of the base, and pour in. After spinning on the Mix-In setting, it’ll turn into perfect, creamy chocolate chips.
- 3g crushed graham cracker
- 5g caramel syrup
329 cal 48g C, 7g F, 24g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
3. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
4. Spin on “Respin” setting if powdery
5. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife and fill with the melted chocolate
6. Run the “Mix-in” cycle
7. Top with the crumbled graham cracker
8. Drizzle with caramel syrup

